("Recognise reductions and liaison","Common words may be shortened and adjacent sounds linked. Listen repeatedly: first for topic, then main clauses, then details."),
("Discourse markers as signposts","Ben, donc, finalement, en fait, bref and cela dit reveal how a speaker organises an idea: reformulation, conclusion, contrast or hesitation."),
("Infer meaning from context","Use topic, grammar, collocations and speaker intention to infer an unfamiliar word. Do not stop listening to translate each word."),
("Accent variation","Quebec French contains diverse accents and styles. Vowel quality, rhythm, affrication and vocabulary vary by region, age and situation."),
("A practical listening cycle","Listen once for the general message; listen again for structure; replay difficult segments; summarise aloud. Check a transcript only after an independent attempt.")
