("Tone and lexical fields","Notice recurring vocabulary, sentence rhythm and formality. A semantic field can create atmosphere or connect images across a passage."),
("Narrative time","A story may use flashback, anticipation, ellipsis or a non-linear sequence. Ask why the writer delays information or shifts chronology."),
("Ambiguity and subtext","A text may imply more than it states. Support interpretations with details and distinguish a plausible reading from certainty."),
("Critical discussion","Summarise briefly, then analyse technique and effect. Plot summary is not a substitute for interpretation; use textual details as evidence.")
